hadiths[392]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O family of Muhammad! Whoever among you performs Hajj, let him also enter ihram for Umrah within his Hajj."
"7812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! Every people has an Eid, and this is our Eid."
"7813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! Say: O Allah, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord and Sovereign of everything, there is no true god except You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self, and from the evil of Satan and his polytheism, and from committing any evil against myself or bringing it upon any Muslim."
"7814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! What do you think of two whose third is Allah?"
"7815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Tha'labah! Whatever (game) your bow, your trained dog and your hand bring back to you, eat it, whether it has been slaughtered or not."
"7816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! Do you think that abundance of wealth is richness (self-sufficiency)? True richness is only the richness of the heart, and true poverty is the poverty of the heart. Whoever has richness in his heart, nothing of this world harms him; and whoever has poverty in his heart, even the abundance of this world does not make him rich; and nothing harms him except the greed of his own self."
"7817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! When you fast three days of the month, then fast the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."
"7818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! When you cook a curry, make plenty of its broth and look after your neighbours."
"7819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! What do you think, if severe hunger afflicts the people, to the point that you cannot even get up from your bed to go to your mosque, what will you do? (He said:) Refrain from asking. O Abu Dharr! What do you think, if severe death befalls the people, to the point that a house (the grave) is obtained for (the price of) a slave, what will you do? (He said:) Be patient. O Abu Dharr! What do you think, if the people kill one another until the stones of al-Zayt are drowned in blood, what will you do? (He said:) Sit in your house and close your door. Abu Dharr said: What if I am not left alone? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then go to those you belong with and be among them. He said: Should I then take up my weapon? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then you would become their partner in that (tribulation) they are in. But if you fear that the gleam of the sword will overwhelm you (and drive you to fight), then throw the edge of your cloak over your face, so that he (the killer) returns bearing his own sin and the sin of killing you, and becomes one of the people of the Fire."
"7820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! Shall I not tell you of a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? It is: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no power to avoid sin and no strength to do good except through Allah)."
"7821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! Shall I not teach you some words which, if you say them, you will catch up with those who have gone ahead of you, and no one will overtake you except one who does the like of your deeds? After every prayer, say Allahu akbar thirty-three times, say Subhan Allah thirty-three times, say Al-hamdu lillah thirty-three times, and conclude with 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; to Him belongs the dominion, to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things). Whoever says that, his sins are forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"7822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! You are a man in whom a trace of the Days of Ignorance remains. These (slaves) are your brothers; Allah has given you precedence over them. So whoever does not suit you, sell him, and do not torment the creation of Allah."
"7823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! You are weak, and this (authority) is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be a cause of disgrace and regret, except for the one who takes it with its right and fulfils what is due from him in it."
"7824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! After me there will be rulers who will kill the prayer (that is, not offer it on time). So offer the prayer at its time; then if you (also) pray (with them) at its time, it will be a voluntary prayer for you; otherwise, you will already have secured your (obligatory) prayer."
"7825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! I see that you are weak, and I love for you what I love for myself: do not become the leader even over two people, and do not take charge of the wealth of an orphan."
"7826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! I would not like to have gold equal to (Mount) Uhud and for three nights to pass while a single dinar of it still remains with me, except a dinar that I keep aside for paying a debt, unless I (distribute) it among the servants of Allah like this, and like this, and like this. O Abu Dharr! Those who have the most (wealth) are the ones with the least (reward), except the one who (spends) it like this and like this."
"7827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! I would not like to have gold equal to (Mount) Uhud and to spend all of it except three dinars."
"7828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! Do you know where the sun goes after it sets? It goes to the Throne and prostrates before its Lord, and asks permission to return, and it is given permission; and it is near that it will be told: Return from where you came, and it will rise from its place of setting. That is its resting place."
"7829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Sa'id! Whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion and with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) as Prophet, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. And there is another thing by which a servant is raised one hundred degrees in Paradise, the distance between every two degrees being like the distance between the heaven and the earth: that thing is jihad in the path of Allah, jihad in the path of Allah."
"7830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Umayr! How is your little bird (nughayr)?"
"7831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Musa! You have indeed been given a melodious voice like the voices of the family of Dawud (peace be upon him)."
"7832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hurayrah! The pen has dried with what you are going to meet. So castrate yourself on that account, or leave it."
"7833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hurayrah! Be scrupulous in piety and you will be among the most devoted worshippers; be content with what Allah has allotted you and you will be among the richest of people; love for the Muslims and the believers what you love for yourself and your household, and dislike for them what you dislike for yourself and your household, and you will be a believer; treat well whoever you live alongside, and you will be a Muslim; and beware of much laughter, for much laughter is a corruption of the heart."
"7834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O son of Adam! Spending your surplus wealth is better for you, and holding on to it is bad for you, and you will not be blamed for keeping what suffices your needs. Begin with those whose support is your responsibility; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"7835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn al-Akwa'! You have prevailed, so be gentle."
"7836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn al-Khasasiyyah! What objection do you have against Allah, when you are walking in the morning alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"
"7837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn al-Khattab! Go and announce among the people that none will enter Paradise except the believers."
"7838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn Hawalah! When you see that the caliphate has settled in the Holy Land, then earthquakes, turmoil and momentous affairs have drawn near, and on that day the Hour will be as close to the people as this hand of mine is to your head."
"7839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn Abis! Shall I not tell you of the best thing with which those who seek refuge seek refuge? It is these two surahs: 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak' (Surah al-Falaq) and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind' (Surah al-Nas)."
"7840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ibn Awf! Mount your horse, then call out: Paradise is lawful only for a believer."
"7841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ubayy! My Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, sent word to me that the Qur'an should be recited in one mode of recitation, so I replied: Make it easy for my Ummah. Then He sent word a second time that it should be recited in two modes, so I again replied: Make it easy for my Ummah. Then He sent word a third time that it should be recited in seven modes, and that for every reply you sent back you have the right to one supplication which you may ask of Me. So I said: O Allah, forgive my Ummah! O Allah, forgive my Ummah! And I have deferred the third supplication for the day on which all of creation will turn to me, even Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"7842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ubayy! The Qur'an has been revealed in seven modes of recitation, each of which is healing and sufficient."
"7843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ubayy! I was taught to recite the Qur'an, and it was said to me: In one mode or in two? The angel who was with me said: Say, in two. I said: In two. Then it was said to me: In two or in three? The angel who was with me said: Say, in three. I said: In three, until it reached seven modes. Then it was said: Each of them is healing and sufficient, whether you say at the end of a verse 'Sami'an Alima' (All-Hearing, All-Knowing) or 'Azizan Hakima' (Almighty, All-Wise), so long as you do not end a verse of punishment with mercy or a verse of mercy with punishment."
"7844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my brothers! Prepare for a day such as this."
"7845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Usamah! Do you intercede regarding one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah?!"
"7846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Usamah! What will you do with 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true god except Allah) when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?!"
"7847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Asma'! When a woman reaches puberty, it is not proper for any part of her to be seen except this and this - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to his face and his two palms."
"7848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ashajj! You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness."
"7849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bedouin! Allah became angry with two tribes of the Children of Israel and transformed them into creatures that creep upon the earth. I do not know; perhaps this (meaning the dabb lizard) is one of them. So I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it."
"7850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best number of companions is four, and the best detachment is four hundred, and the best army is four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated on account of small numbers."
"7851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm al-Ala'! Rejoice, for through the illness of a Muslim Allah removes his sins just as fire removes the dross of gold and silver."
"7852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Harithah! There are many gardens in Paradise, and your son has attained al-Firdaws al-A'la (the highest Firdaws), and Firdaws is the highest, most central and most excellent place in Paradise."
"7853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Harithah! It is not one Paradise; rather, there are many Paradises, and Harithah is in al-Firdaws al-A'la (the highest Firdaws)."
"7854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Salamah! The heart of every human being is between two of the fingers of Allah; whomever He wills He keeps upright, and whomever He wills He causes to deviate."
"7855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Salamah! Do not hurt me concerning Aishah, for by Allah, revelation has never come down to me while I was under the blanket of any woman among you except her."
"7856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Sulaym! Do you not know that I made a stipulation with my Lord and said: I am only a human being; I become pleased as human beings become pleased, and I become angry as human beings become angry. So whoever from my Ummah I have invoked against, and he did not deserve it, then O Allah, make it for him a purification, a cleansing and a means of nearness by which You bring him near to Yourself on the Day of Resurrection."
"7857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O mother of so-and-so! Sit in whichever corner of the streets you wish, and I will come and sit with you."
"7858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Anjashah! Slow down your driving, for these are women as delicate as glass."
"7859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Anas! People will build new cities, and one of them will be called Basrah or Busayrah. If you pass by it or enter it, then beware of its salt marshes, its pastures, its marketplace and the gates of its rulers, and keep to its outskirts, for there will be sinking into the earth, pelting (with stones) and earthquakes there, and some people will go to sleep at night and wake up in the morning as apes and swine."
"7860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people of the Qur'an! Pray witr, for Allah loves witr."
"7861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Fear Allah, and even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed as your ruler, listen to him and obey, as long as he establishes the Book of Allah among you."
"7862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Fear your Lord who created you from a single soul, and created from it its mate, and from the two of them spread many men and women. And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and fear (severing) the ties of kinship. Indeed, Allah is ever Watchful over you. O you who believe! Fear Allah, and let every soul look to what it has sent forward for tomorrow, and fear Allah; indeed, Allah is fully Aware of what you do. Let a man give in charity from his dinar, from his dirham, from his garment, from his sa' of wheat, from his sa' of dates, even if it is only half a date."
"7863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Remember Allah, remember Allah! The first quake has come, to be followed by the second; the first quake has come, to be followed by the second. Death has come with all that it brings."
"7864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Be gentle with yourselves, for you are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent; rather, you are calling upon One who is All-Hearing and Near, and He is with you."
"7865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Spread the greeting of peace (salam), feed others, maintain the ties of kinship, and pray at night while people are asleep, and you will enter Paradise in peace."
"7866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! The sun and the moon are two of the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death or the life of anyone. So when you see any of that, pray until it clears. I have seen, in this very prayer of mine, everything that you have been promised. Hell was brought forward, and that was when you saw me step back for fear that its blast would reach me, until I said: O Lord, and I am among them? And in it I saw the man with the crooked staff dragging his intestines in the Fire; he used to steal from the pilgrims with his staff, and if he was caught he would say: It just got caught on my staff! And if people were unaware, he would take it away. And I even saw in it the woman of the cat, who tied it up and neither fed it nor let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth, until it died of hunger. And Paradise was brought forward, and that was when you saw me step forward until I stood in my place, and I stretched out my hand wanting to take some of its fruit so that you could look at it; then it occurred to me not to do so."
"7867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Allah has removed from you the arrogance of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah) and its habit of boasting about forefathers. People are of two kinds: one righteous, God-fearing and honoured in the sight of Allah, and the other wicked, wretched and lowly in the sight of Allah. All people are the children of Adam, and Allah created Adam from dust."
"7868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Some of you drive people away. So whoever leads the people in prayer, let him keep it short, for behind him are the weak, the elderly and the one who has some need."
"7869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! This is from your spoils of war. Return even the thread and the needle, and whatever is above that, for misappropriation (of spoils) will be disgrace, dishonour and fire for the one who does it on the Day of Resurrection."
"7870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! You will be gathered before Allah barefoot, naked and uncircumcised. As We began the first creation, so shall We repeat it. Behold! The first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim (peace be upon him). Behold! Some men from my Ummah will be brought and taken towards the left, and I will say: O Lord, these are my companions! And it will be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you. Then I will say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them, but when You took me up, You were the Watcher over them. Then it will be said: These people did not cease turning back on their heels in apostasy from the time you parted from them."
"7871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! You will not be able to do everything I have commanded you, but stay on the right course, keep close to it, and rejoice."
"7872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Of what Allah has given you as spoils, not even the equivalent of this small thing is lawful for me except the fifth, and that fifth too is returned to you."
"7873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Nothing of these spoils is lawful for me, not even this - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to a hair from the hump of a camel - except the fifth, and that fifth too is returned to you. So return even the needle and the thread."
"7874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! The Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) was made clear to me, and I came out to tell you about it, but two men came quarrelling and Satan was with them, so I was made to forget its fixed date. So seek it in the last ten nights of Ramadan; seek it on the ninth, the seventh and the fifth nights."
"7875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Since Allah created the offspring of Adam (peace be upon him), there has been no trial on the face of the earth greater than the trial of the Dajjal. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has not sent any prophet except that he warned his Ummah about the Dajjal. I am the last of the prophets and you are the last of the nations, and he will inevitably appear among you. If he emerges while I am among you, I will argue on behalf of every Muslim; and if he emerges after me, then each person will argue on his own behalf, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. He will emerge from a path between Syria and Iraq and will spread corruption to the right and to the left. O servants of Allah! O people! Stand firm, for I will describe him to you with a description that no prophet before me has given. He will say: I am your Lord, yet you will not see your Lord until you die. He is one-eyed, whereas your Lord is not one-eyed, and between his two eyes is written: Kafir (disbeliever), which every believer will read, whether he can write or not. Among his trials is that he will have with him a Paradise and a Hell, but his Hell is in reality Paradise and his Paradise is in reality Hell. So whoever is afflicted with his Hell, let him seek help from Allah and recite the opening verses of Surah al-Kahf. Among his trials is that he will say to a Bedouin: Tell me, if I bring your father and your mother back to life for you, will you bear witness that I am your Lord? He will say: Yes. Then two devils will appear to him in the form of his father and his mother and say: O my son, follow him, for he is your Lord. Among his trials is that he will be given power over one person, and he will kill him, sawing him with a saw until he falls in two pieces. Then he will say: Look at this servant of mine; I will now bring him back to life, and then he will claim that he has a Lord other than me. So Allah will bring him back to life, and the wicked one will say to him: Who is your Lord? He will say: My Lord is Allah, and you are the enemy of Allah, the Dajjal. By Allah, I never recognised you as clearly before as I do today. Among his trials is that he will command the sky to rain and it will rain, and command the earth to grow vegetation and it will grow. Among his trials is that he will pass by a tribe and they will reject him, and all their grazing livestock will perish. And among his trials is that he will pass by a tribe and they will believe him, and he will command the sky to rain and it will rain, and command the earth to grow vegetation and it will grow, until their livestock return that very evening fatter, larger, fuller in the flanks and more abundant in milk than they ever were. There will be no part of the earth that he does not reach and prevail over, except Makkah and Madinah; he will not approach them by any of their paths except that angels will meet him with drawn swords, until he halts near the red mound at the far edge of the salt plain. Then Madinah will shake with its inhabitants three times, and no hypocrite, man or woman, will remain in it except that he goes out to him. Thus Madinah will expel its impure ones just as the furnace removes the dross of iron, and that day will be called the Day of Deliverance. It was asked: Where will the Arabs be at that time? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On that day they will be few, and their imam will be a righteous man. While their imam has stepped forward to lead them in the Fajr prayer, Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon them both) will descend at the time of Fajr. That imam will begin to step back so that Isa (peace be upon him) may go forward, but Isa (peace be upon him) will place his hand between his shoulders and say to him: Go forward and lead the prayer, for it was established for you. So their imam will lead them in prayer, and when he finishes, Isa (peace be upon him) will say: Open the gate. They will open it, and behind it will be the Dajjal, with seventy thousand Jews, each with an ornamented sword and a shield. When the Dajjal sees Isa (peace be upon him), he will begin to dissolve as salt dissolves in water, and he will run away. Isa (peace be upon him) will catch up with him at the eastern gate of Ludd and kill him. Then Allah will defeat the Jews, and there will be nothing behind which a Jew hides except that Allah will make that thing speak, whether stone, tree, wall or animal, except the gharqad tree, for it is one of their trees and will not speak. Everything else will say: O Muslim servant of Allah! Here is a Jew; come and kill him. Then Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon them both) will be among my Ummah a just judge and an equitable leader. He will break the cross, slaughter the swine, abolish the jizyah and leave the charity, so zakah will not be collected on sheep or on camels. Rancour and mutual hatred will be lifted, and the venom of every venomous creature will be removed, until a little boy will put his hand into the mouth of a snake and it will not harm him, and a little girl will harm a lion and it will not harm her, and the wolf will be among the sheep as though it were their guard dog. The earth will be filled with peace as a vessel is filled with water, and the word of all will be one, so that none will be worshipped except Allah. War will lay down its burdens, and Quraysh will be stripped of their kingship. The earth will become like a silver platter, clean and clear, and will grow its produce as it did in the time of Adam (peace be upon him), until a group of people will gather to eat one bunch of grapes and it will satisfy them, and a group will gather to eat one pomegranate and it will satisfy them. An ox will be worth such-and-such an amount of wealth, and a horse will be worth a few dirhams. Before the emergence of the Dajjal there will be three hard years in which people will be struck by severe hunger. Allah will command the sky in the first year to withhold a third of its rain and command the earth to withhold a third of its produce. Then in the second year He will command the sky and it will withhold two thirds of its rain, and He will command the earth and it will withhold two thirds of its produce. Then in the third year He will command the sky and it will withhold all of its rain, so that not a single drop falls, and He will command the earth and it will withhold all of its produce, so that no green thing grows. Then no hoofed animal will survive, except whatever Allah wills; they will all perish. It was asked: How then will people live at that time? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the remembrance of 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no god but Allah), 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) and 'Al-hamdu lillah' (praise be to Allah), which will suffice them as food does."
"7876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing (ruku'), nor in prostration, nor in standing, nor in sitting, nor in ending the prayer, for I see you in front of me and behind me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much."
"7877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! I am leaving among you two things; if you hold fast to them, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my 'itrah, that is, my family (Ahl al-Bayt)."
"7878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! I had permitted you to contract temporary marriage (mut'ah) with women, and now Allah has made it unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever has any such woman with him by way of mut'ah, let him release her, and do not take back anything of what you have given them."
"7879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Whoever among the believers is struck by a calamity, let him find consolation for that calamity through the calamity of my death, for no one from my Ummah will ever be struck, after me, by a calamity harder upon him than the calamity of losing me."
"7880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Which day is the most sacred? Which day is the most sacred? Which day is the most sacred? The Companions said: The day of the greater Hajj. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then your blood, your wealth and your honour are sacred to you, just as this day of yours is sacred, in this city of yours, in this month of yours. Behold! No wrongdoer brings the consequence of his crime upon anyone but himself. Behold! No father is answerable for the crime of his child, nor a child for the crime of his father. Behold! Satan has despaired of ever being worshipped in this city of yours, but he will succeed in being obeyed in some of your deeds that you regard as insignificant, and he will be content with that. Behold! A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim, and nothing belonging to his brother is lawful for a Muslim except what he gives willingly. Behold! All usury (riba) of the Days of Ignorance is abolished; you shall have your capital sums, neither wronging nor being wronged, except the usury of Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib, which is also abolished entirely. And every blood claim of the Days of Ignorance is waived, and the first blood claim of the Days of Ignorance that I waive is that of al-Harith bin Abd al-Muttalib. Behold! Accept my counsel to treat women well, for they are like captives with you; you have no authority over them beyond that, unless they commit open indecency. If they do so, then leave them alone in their beds and strike them lightly, without causing injury. Then if they obey you, do not seek any means against them. Behold! You have a right over your women, and your women have a right over you. Your right over them is that they do not allow anyone you dislike onto your beds, and that they do not admit anyone you dislike into your houses. Behold! Their right over you is that you treat them well in their clothing and their food."
"7881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Repent to your Lord, for by Allah, I repent to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, a hundred times a day."
"7882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Learn your Hajj rites from me, for I do not know; perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this year of mine."
"7883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Return my cloak to me. By Allah, if I had livestock as many as the trees of Tihamah, I would distribute them among you, and then you would not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar. O people! Nothing of these spoils is lawful for me, not even the equivalent of this hair, except the fifth, and that fifth too is returned to you. So return even the needle and the thread, for misappropriation (of spoils) will be disgrace, fire and dishonour for the one who does it on the Day of Resurrection."
"7884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Keep calm, for righteousness does not lie in making horses and camels run fast."
"7885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Keep calm and dignified, for righteousness does not lie in making camels run fast."
"7886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Adopt moderation, adopt moderation, adopt moderation, for Allah Almighty will not grow weary of rewarding until you grow weary of doing deeds."
"7887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Do only as many deeds as you are able to, for Allah does not grow weary of rewarding until you grow weary of doing deeds, and the deed most beloved to Allah is the one done consistently, even if it is little."
"7888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! What is the matter with you that when something happens to you in the prayer, you start clapping? Clapping is only for women. Whoever has something happen to him in his prayer, let him say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), for when someone says 'Subhan Allah', whoever hears him turns his attention to him."
"7889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Do you know why I have gathered you? By Allah, I have not gathered you for any hope or fear, but I have gathered you because Tamim al-Dari - who was a Christian, then came, gave the pledge of allegiance and became Muslim - told me something that agrees with what I used to tell you about the Masih al-Dajjal. He told me that he boarded a seagoing ship with thirty men from Lakhm and Judham, and the waves tossed them about in the sea for a month. Then they came to shore at an island in the sea at sunset, and they sat in the ship's small boats and entered the island. There they met a very hairy beast, with so much hair that its front could not be told from its back. They said: Woe to you, what are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They asked: What is al-Jassasah? It said: O people, go to this man in the monastery, for he is very eager for news of you. Tamim said: When it named a man to us, we became afraid of it, lest it be a she-devil itself. So we went quickly until we entered the gate of the monastery, and there was the largest human being we had ever seen, and the most tightly bound, his two hands tied to his neck and, between his knees and his ankles, chains of iron. We asked: Woe to you, what are you? He said: You are able to learn my news; first tell me who you are. We said: We are some people of the Arabs. We boarded a seagoing ship, the sea became rough, and the waves tossed us about for a month. Then we came to shore at this island of yours, and we sat in the ship's small boats and entered the island. There we met a very hairy beast, with so much hair that its front could not be told from its back. We said: Woe to you, what are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. We asked: What is al-Jassasah? It said: Go to this man in the monastery, for he is eager for news of you. So we came to you quickly, afraid of it and not feeling safe that it might be a she-devil. He said: Tell me about the date palms of Baysan. We asked: What do you want to know about them? He said: I am asking you whether they bear fruit. We said: Yes. He said: Behold! Soon they will stop bearing fruit. He said: Tell me about the lake of Tiberias. We asked: What do you want to know about it? He said: Is there water in it? We said: It has a great deal of water. He said: Soon its water will be gone. He said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar. We asked: What do you want to know about it? He said: Is there water in the spring? And do its people cultivate with the water of the spring? We said: Yes, it has a great deal of water, and its people cultivate with its water. He said: Tell me about the Prophet of the unlettered people; what has he done? We said: He has left Makkah and settled in Yathrib. He asked: Have the Arabs fought him? We said: Yes. He asked: What did he do with the Arabs? So we told him that he had prevailed over the Arabs near him and that they had submitted to him in obedience. He said: Has that really happened? We said: Yes. He said: It is better for them to obey him. And now I will tell you about myself: I am the Masih al-Dajjal, and soon I will be given permission to emerge. Then I will emerge and travel through the earth, and I will not leave a single town without descending upon it within forty nights, except Makkah and Madinah; both of them are forbidden to me. Whenever I want to enter either of them, an angel with a drawn sword in his hand will meet me and turn me back, and on every path to them there are angels guarding them. Shall I not tell you? This is Madinah, this is Madinah, this is Madinah. Had I not told you this before? Tamim's account pleased me because it agrees with what I told you about him, and about Madinah and Makkah. Behold! He is in the sea of Syria, or in the sea of Yemen; no, rather he will come from the direction of the east, he is from the direction of the east, he is from the direction of the east."
"7890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Do not kill one another and do not harm one another, and when you stone the Jamrah, throw pebbles the size of small flicking pebbles."
"7891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not stand until you see me."
"7892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bilal! Establish the prayer; give us rest through it."
"7893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bilal! Stand and announce: None will enter Paradise except a believer, and Allah supports this religion even through a wicked man."
"7894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bilal! By what deed did you get ahead of me into Paradise? Whenever I entered Paradise, I heard the sound of your sandals ahead of me. Last night I entered Paradise and heard the sound of your sandals ahead of me. Then I came to a square, lofty palace of gold, and I asked: 'Whose palace is this?' It was said: 'A man of Quraysh.' I said: 'I am a Qurashi; whose palace is this?' It was said: 'A man from the Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' I said: 'I am Muhammad; whose palace is this?' It was said: 'Umar bin al-Khattab's.'"
"7895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O daughter of Abu Umayyah! You asked about the two rak'ahs after Asr. Some people from the tribe of Abd al-Qays came to me and kept me occupied from the two rak'ahs after Zuhr, so these are those two."
"7896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Bayadah! Marry your daughters to Abu Hind, and marry your sons into his family."
"7897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Salimah! Do you not count the reward of your footsteps to the mosque?"
"7898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Salimah! Stay in your homes; your footsteps are recorded."
"7899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Giving water to the pilgrims will remain your task, and were it not for the fear that people would overpower you in it, I myself would draw water along with you."
"7900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Abd Manaf! Do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House (the Ka'bah) and praying at whatever hour he wishes, of night or day."
"7901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Abd Manaf! O Banu Abd Manaf! I am a warner to you. The likeness of me and you is that of a man who saw the enemy and ran to warn his family, and he feared that the enemy would reach his family before him, so he began to cry out: 'Beware! Beware! The enemy has come, the enemy has come!'"
"7902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Fihr! O Banu Adi! O Banu Abd Manaf! O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Tell me, if I were to inform you that there is a cavalry in the valley that wants to attack you, would you believe me?"" They said: ""We have found nothing in you but truthfulness."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then I am a warner to you ahead of a severe punishment."
"7903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Ka'b bin Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Murrah bin Ka'b! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd Shams! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah! Save yourself from the Fire, for I have no power to avail you anything against Allah, except that you are my kin, whose right I will fulfil in this world."
"7904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Jabir! If the garment is wide, cross its two ends over your shoulders in opposite directions, and if it is narrow, tie it around your waist."
"7905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Jabir! Shall I not give you the glad tidings of how Allah met your father? Allah has never spoken to anyone except from behind a veil, except your father; He spoke to him face to face and said: 'O My servant! Ask of Me, and I will give you.' He said: 'O my Lord! Bring me back to life so that I may be martyred in Your path a second time.' Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, said: 'It has already been decreed by Me that they will not return after death.' He said: 'O Lord! Then convey this to those I have left behind in the world.'"
"7906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Jarhad! Cover your thigh, for the thigh too is awrah (a part that must be covered)."
"7907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Hazim! Say often 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (there is no power to avoid sins nor strength to do good deeds except through the help of Allah), for it is one of the treasures of Paradise."
"7908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Hassan! Reply on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit (Ruh al-Qudus)."
"7909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O you of the two ears!"
"7910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ruwayfi'! Perhaps your life will be long after me, so inform the people that whoever ties knots in his beard, or wears a bowstring as an amulet, or cleans himself after relieving himself with animal dung or a bone, then Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is free of him."
"7911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Sa'd! Shoot, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you."
"7912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Sa'd! I give to a man while someone else is dearer to me than him, out of fear that Allah may throw him on his face into Hell."
"7913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O you with the leather sandals! Woe to you! Take off your sandals."
"7914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib! O Fatimah bint Muhammad! O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! I have no power to avail you anything against Allah; ask me for whatever you wish of my wealth."
"7915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! This is Jibril, who is conveying his greetings of peace to you."
"7916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this (the moon), for this is the darkening one (al-ghasiq) when it overspreads."
"7917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Did you know that Allah has answered me concerning what I asked Him? Two men came to me; one sat at my head and the other at my feet. The one at my head said to the one at my feet: 'What is this man's ailment?' He said: 'He has been bewitched.' He asked: 'Who bewitched him?' He said: 'Labid bin al-A'sam.' He asked: 'In what thing was it hidden?' He said: 'In a comb, hair, and the husk of a male date-palm spathe.' He asked: 'Where is it?' He said: 'In the well of Dharwan.' O Aishah! By Allah, it was as if its water were the water in which henna is steeped, and as if its date palms were the heads of devils."
"7918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Was there no entertainment with you? For the Ansar like entertainment."
"7919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Allah created people for Paradise; He created them for it while they were in the loins of their fathers. And He created people for Hell; He created them for it while they were in the loins of their fathers."
"7920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness in every matter."
"7921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Allah is Gentle, He loves gentleness, and He grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness, and what He does not grant for anything else."
"7922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Allah does not love the foul-mouthed and the one who deliberately indulges in obscenity."
"7923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! The worst of people are those who are honoured only to guard against their evil."
"7924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! My eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"7925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Among the worst of people is the one whom people leave alone to guard against his foul tongue."
"7926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Remove this from here, for whenever I come in and see it, I am reminded of the world."
"7927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Hold fast to the fear of Allah and adopt gentleness, for gentleness is never in anything except that it adorns it, and it is never removed from anything except that it disfigures it."
"7928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Were it not that your people have only recently come out of the Jahiliyyah (the Days of Ignorance), I would have demolished the Ka'bah and included in it the part that was taken out of it, made it level with the ground, and given it two doors, one to the east and one to the west, and I would have brought it to the foundations of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"7929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! I still feel the pain of the food I ate at Khaybar, and now is the time when I feel my main artery being cut because of that poison."
"7930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! What assures me that there is no punishment in this cloud? A people were punished with the wind, and a people saw the punishment and said: 'This is a cloud that will bring us rain.'"
"7931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! When have you ever found me foul-mouthed? The worst of people in rank with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people leave alone to guard against his evil."
"7932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Do not keep count when giving charity, or else Allah will also keep count of His giving to you."
"7933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Do not be foul-mouthed."
"7934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Seek treatment, for Allah has not created any disease without also creating a cure for it, except for one disease: old age."
"7935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Allah has removed hardship, except for the one who unjustly attacks the honour of a Muslim; it is he who falls into hardship and is ruined."
"7936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abbas! Are you not amazed at Mughith's love for Barirah and Barirah's hatred for Mughith?"
"7937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abbas! O my uncle! Shall I not give you something? Shall I not grant you something? Shall I not present you with a gift? Shall I not tell you of ten things which, if you do them, Allah will forgive your sins, the first and the last, the old and the new, the unintentional and the deliberate, the small and the great, the hidden and the open? These ten things are: you pray four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah Surah al-Fatihah and another surah. Then, when you have finished the recitation in the first rak'ah while standing, say fifteen times: 'Subhan Allah, wal-hamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu akbar' (Glory be to Allah, all praise is for Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest). Then bow, and say it ten times while bowing. Then raise your head from bowing and say it ten times. Then go down in prostration and say it ten times while prostrating. Then raise your head from prostration and say it ten times. Then prostrate a second time and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. That makes seventy-five in each rak'ah; do this in four rak'ahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of the desert, Allah would forgive them. If you can, pray it once every day; if you cannot, then once every Friday; if you cannot, then once every month; if you cannot, then once every year; and if you cannot, then be sure to pray it once in your lifetime."
"7938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abbas! O uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"7939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abd al-Rahman! Take your sister and have her perform Umrah from al-Tan'im."
"7940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abd al-Rahman! Seat your sister Aishah behind you and have her perform Umrah from al-Tan'im, and when you descend with her from the hillock, tell her to enter the state of ihram, for it will be an accepted Umrah."
"7941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah! Do not ask for leadership, for if it is given to you because you asked for it, you will be left to it on your own; and if it is given to you without your asking, you will be helped in it by Allah. And when you swear an oath and then see something else better than it, make expiation for your oath and do what is better."
"7942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah! Have I not been told that you fast during the day and stand in prayer at night? Do not do so, for if you do that, your eyes will become sunken and your body will grow weak. Fast and also break your fast, stand in prayer and also rest, for your body has a right over you, your eyes have a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. It is sufficient for you to fast three days every month, for the reward of every good deed is ten times its like, so that will be equal to fasting perpetually."" He said: I have the strength for more than that. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then fast the fast of the Prophet of Allah Dawud (peace be upon him) and do not do more than that; it is equal to fasting half of one's life."
"7943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah! If Allah admits you into Paradise, all of this will be yours, along with whatever your heart desires and whatever delights your eye."
"7944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah bin Qays! Shall I not tell you of a phrase which is one of the treasures of Paradise? It is: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no power to avoid sin and no strength to do good except from Allah)."
"7945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah! Do not be like so-and-so; he used to stand in prayer at night, then he abandoned the night prayer."
"7946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uthman! Have you turned away from my way?! I sleep and I pray, I fast and I break my fast, and I marry women. O Uthman! Fear Allah, for your family has a right over you, your guest has a right over you, and your own self has a right over you. So fast and also break your fast, pray and also rest."
"7947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uthman! Allah will clothe you with a shirt, so if the hypocrites try to force you to take it off, do not take it off until you come to meet me."
"7948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uqbah! Shall I not teach you the two best surahs that have ever been recited? 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind'. O Uqbah! Recite them every time you go to sleep and every time you get up. No one who asks has ever asked by anything like them, and no one who seeks refuge has ever sought refuge by anything like them."
"7949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uqbah bin Amir! Seek refuge with these two, for no one who seeks refuge has ever sought refuge by anything like them."
"7950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uqbah! 'Say: He is Allah, the One', 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind'; no one has ever sought refuge by anything like them."
"7951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ali! Are you not pleased that your position in relation to me is like that of Harun (peace be upon him) in relation to Musa (peace be upon him)? Except that there is no prophet after me."
"7952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ali! Ask Allah for guidance and for being on target. When you pray for guidance, keep in mind being guided straight along a road, and when you pray for being on target, keep in mind an arrow hitting its mark."
"7953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ali! Do not follow one glance with another, for the first glance is forgiven for you, but the second is not permitted for you."
"7954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ali! Do not sit on your buttocks like a dog."
"7955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O uncle! Shall I not give you something? Shall I not give you a gift? Shall I not benefit you? O uncle! Pray four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah Surah al-Fatihah and another surah. Then, when the recitation is finished, say fifteen times before bowing: 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest), 'wal-hamdu lillah' (and all praise is for Allah), 'wa subhan Allah' (and glory be to Allah) and 'wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is no god but Allah). Then bow and say it ten times before raising your head; then raise your head and say it ten times before prostrating; then prostrate and say it ten times before raising your head; then raise your head and say it ten times; then make the second prostration and say it ten times; then raise your head and say it ten times before standing up. That makes seventy-five in each rak'ah, and three hundred in four rak'ahs. Then even if your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of the desert, Allah would forgive them for you. If you are unable to pray it every day, then pray it every Friday; if you cannot do that, then pray it every month; and if you cannot do that, then pray it every year."
"7956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Awf! Remember six things before the Hour: first, my death; then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis; then an epidemic that will spread among you, through which Allah will grant martyrdom to your offspring and yourselves and will purify your wealth; then wealth will become so abundant among you that a man will be given a hundred dinars and still remain displeased; then a tribulation will arise among you that will not leave a single Muslim home without entering it; then there will be a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar, but they will betray it and march against you under eighty banners, with twelve thousand soldiers under each banner."
"7957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O boy! I will teach you some words: Guard (the rights of) Allah and Allah will guard you; guard (the rights of) Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah alone, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah alone. And know that if the entire nation gathered together to benefit you with something, they could benefit you only with what Allah has already written for you; and if they all gathered together to harm you with something, they could harm you only with what Allah has already written against you. The pens have dried and the scrolls have been lifted."
"7958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O boy! Say Bismillah (in the name of Allah), eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"7959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O boy! This is your father and this is your mother; take the hand of whichever of the two you wish."
"7960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah! Shave this child's head and give in charity silver equal to the weight of his hair."
"7961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah! Are you not pleased to be the leader of the believing women?"
"7962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah! Would it please you for people to say that Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad, has a chain of fire in her hand?!"
"7963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O so-and-so! Which would be more beloved to you: that you enjoy him (your child) throughout your life, or that tomorrow you do not come to any of the gates of Paradise except that you find he has gone ahead of you to it, opening it for you?"
"7964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O so-and-so! Can you not perform your prayer properly? Does the one who prays not look at how he is praying? He is only praying for his own sake. By Allah! I see behind me just as I see in front of me."
"7965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Qabisah! Asking (for help) is lawful only for one of three people: a man who has taken upon himself a financial liability (blood money) for the sake of reconciliation; asking is lawful for him until he pays it off, then he should stop. Second, a man who has been struck by a calamity that has destroyed all his wealth; asking is lawful for him until he obtains enough to live on. Third, a man who has been afflicted by such destitution that three sensible people from his people testify that so-and-so has been afflicted by destitution; then asking is lawful for him until he obtains enough to live on, then he should stop. Asking other than this is unlawful, and the one who asks consumes unlawful wealth."
"7966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! Are you one who causes trouble (fitnah)? Why did you not lead the prayer reciting 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', 'By the sun and its morning brightness' or 'By the night when it covers'? For behind you pray the old, the weak and the one who has some need."
"7967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh bin Jabal! Whoever testifies sincerely from his heart that 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah) and that I am the Messenger of Allah, Allah makes him forbidden for the Fire."" Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall I not tell the people so that they may rejoice? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then they would give up deeds and rely on this alone."
"7968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh bin Jabal! Do you know what the right of Allah over His servants is, and what the right of the servants over Allah is? The right of Allah over the servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and the right of the servants over Allah is that He does not punish anyone who does not associate anything with Him."
"7969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! By Allah, I love you. I advise you, O Mu'adh: never leave off saying after every prayer: 'Allahumma a'inni 'ala dhikrika wa shukrika wa husni 'ibadatik' (O Allah, help me to remember You, to thank You and to worship You in the best manner)."
"7970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ansar! Did I not find you astray, and then Allah guided you through me? And you were divided, and then Allah united you through me? And you were poor, and then Allah made you rich through me? Are you not pleased that the people should go away with sheep and camels while you take the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) back to your homes? Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been one of the Ansar; and if the people were to go through a valley and a mountain pass, I would go through the valley and mountain pass of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner garment and the rest of the people are the outer garment. After me you will face others being preferred over you in your rights, so be patient until you meet me at the Pond (Hawd)."
"7971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ansar! Keep your wealth for yourselves and do not give it away as 'umra (a lifetime grant), for whoever gives something as 'umra for a lifetime, it becomes the property of the one it was given to, both in his life and after his death."
"7972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ansar! What is this that has reached me about you? Are you not pleased that the people should go away with wealth while you go away with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), until you bring him into your homes? If all the people took one mountain pass and the Ansar took another, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"7973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O traders! Shaytan and sin are present in buying and selling, so mix your buying and selling with charity."
"7974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O traders! Idle talk and oaths are present in this buying and selling, so mix it with charity."
"7975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O young men! Whoever among you is able to marry, let him marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and in guarding the private parts. And whoever is not able, let him fast, for it is for him like castration in breaking desire."
"7976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O poor people! Shall I not give you glad tidings? The poor among the believers will enter Paradise half a day before their rich, and that half day will be five hundred years."
"7977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Muslims! There is no prayer for the one who does not keep his back straight in bowing and prostration."
"7978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Muhajirun! There are five things; if you are afflicted with them, and I seek refuge with Allah lest you should encounter them, great harm will follow: Whenever immorality spreads among a people to the extent that they commit it openly, plague and diseases spread among them which never existed among their predecessors who passed away before them. And those who give short measure and weight are seized with famine, severe hardship and the tyranny of their rulers. And those who withhold the zakah of their wealth have the rain from the sky withheld from them, and were it not for the animals, they would receive no rain at all. And those who break the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, Allah sets over them an enemy from outside their own people who seizes some of what is in their hands. And those whose rulers do not judge according to the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and do not reflect upon what Allah has revealed, Allah causes them to fight against one another."
"7979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O company of the Muhajirun and the Ansar! Among your brothers are people who have neither wealth nor family, so let each one of you take two or three men with him."
"7980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O women! Give charity and seek forgiveness abundantly, for I have seen that you make up the majority of the people of Hell. You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion who overpowers the mind of a sensible man more than you. As for the deficiency in intellect, it is that the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man; this is the deficiency in intellect. And the deficiency in religion is that you spend several nights without praying and do not fast in Ramadan; this is the deficiency in religion."
"7981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O women! Give charity, even if it is from your jewellery, for you will make up the majority of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."
"7982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people of Quraysh! Save yourselves from the punishment of Allah; I cannot avail you anything against Allah. O Banu Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from Allah; I cannot avail you anything against Allah. O Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib! I cannot avail you anything against Allah. O Safiyyah, aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I cannot avail you anything against Allah. O Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad! Ask me for whatever you wish of my wealth, but I cannot avail you anything against Allah."
"7983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people of Quraysh! Save yourselves from the Fire, for I have no power to cause you harm or benefit against Allah. O people of Banu Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from the Fire, for I have no power to cause you harm or benefit against Allah. O people of Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire, for I have no power to cause you harm or benefit. O Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad! Save yourself from the Fire, for I have no power to cause you harm or benefit. However, you are my kin, and I will fulfil the right of that kinship in this world."
"7984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O you who have believed with your tongues while faith has not entered your hearts! Do not backbite the Muslims and do not pry into their faults, for whoever pries into the faults of his Muslim brother, Allah will pry into his faults, and whoever Allah pries into his faults, He will disgrace him, even if he is inside his own house."
"7985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O you who have become Muslims with your tongues while faith has not entered your hearts! Do not harm the Muslims, do not taunt them and do not pry into their faults, for whoever pries into the faults of his Muslim brother, Allah will pry into his faults, and whoever Allah pries into his faults, He will disgrace him, even if he is inside his own tent."
"7986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O company of Jews! Accept Islam and you will be safe. Know that the land belongs to Allah and His Messenger, and I intend to expel you from this land. So whoever among you finds something in exchange for his property, let him sell it; otherwise, know that the land belongs to Allah and His Messenger."
"7987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Turner of hearts! Keep my heart firm upon Your religion."
"7988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Turner of hearts! Keep our hearts firm upon Your religion."
"7989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Muslim women! Let no neighbour look down upon (the gift of) her neighbour, even if it is only the hoof of a sheep."
"7990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Hazzal! Had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you."
"7991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will come to Madinah and find the angels guarding it, so, if Allah Almighty wills, neither the Dajjal nor the plague will enter it."
"7992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will come, and it will be forbidden for him to enter any of the mountain passes of Madinah, so he will halt in one of the salty plains near Madinah. On that day a man who is the best of people, or one of the best of people, will come out to him and say to him: 'I bear witness that you are the Dajjal about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) told us.' The Dajjal will say: 'Tell me, if I kill this man and then bring him back to life, will you have any doubt about the matter?' The people will say: 'No.' So he will kill him and then bring him back to life, and when he is brought back to life the man will say: 'By Allah, I have never had clearer insight about you than I have today.' Then the Dajjal will want to kill him again, but he will not be given power over him."
"7993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Satan comes to one of you and says: 'Who created such-and-such? Who created such-and-such?' until he says: 'Who created your Lord?' So when this whisper reaches him, let him seek refuge with Allah and stop at that thought."
"7994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an will come along with its people who used to act upon it in the world, led by Surah al-Baqarah and Al Imran. The two of them will come as though they were two clouds with light between them, or as though they were two black clouds, or as though they were two flocks of birds with outspread wings, and the two of them will plead on behalf of the one who recited them."
"7995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Masih al-Dajjal will come from the direction of the east, intending to attack Madinah, until he halts behind Uhud. Then the angels will turn his face towards Sham, and there he will perish."
"7996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from the people of Paradise will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: 'O son of Adam! How did you find your abode?' He will say: 'O Lord! The best of abodes.' Allah will say: 'Ask and wish.' He will say: 'O Lord! I do not ask for anything, nor do I wish for anything, except that You send me back to the world so that I may be killed in Your path ten times,' because of the excellence of martyrdom he sees. And a man from the people of Hell will be brought, and it will be said to him: 'O son of Adam! How did you find your abode?' He will say: 'O Lord! The worst of abodes.' Allah will say: 'Would you ransom yourself from it with the earth's fill of gold?' He will say: 'O Lord! Yes.' Allah will say: 'You have lied. I asked of you something less and easier than that, but you did not do it.' So he will be returned to Hell."
"7997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: 'Did I not give you hearing, sight, wealth and children? Did I not subject cattle and crops to you? Did I not give you leadership and a life of ease? So did you believe that you would meet this Day of yours?' He will say: 'No.' Then Allah will say: 'Today I will forget you just as you forgot Me.'"
"7998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Death will be brought in the form of a black-and-white ram until it is made to stand on the wall between Paradise and Hell. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise!' and they will crane their necks to look. And it will be said: 'O people of Hell!' and they too will crane their necks to look. Then it will be said: 'Do you recognise this?' They will say: 'Yes, this is death.' Then it will be laid down and slaughtered. So had Allah not decreed eternal life for the people of Paradise, they would have died of joy, and had Allah not decreed eternal life in it for the people of Hell, they would have died of grief."
"7999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand on the Sirat. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise!' and they will look out, frightened and fearful that they may be taken out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: 'O people of Hell!' and they will look out, happy and hopeful that they may be taken out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: 'Do you recognise this?' They will say: 'Yes, this is death.' Then a command will be given concerning it and it will be slaughtered on the Sirat. Then it will be said to both groups: 'Now there is eternity in the state you are in; there will never be death in it.'"
"8000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one of the people of Hell who enjoyed the most luxury in the world will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and dipped once into Hell. Then it will be said to him: 'O son of Adam! Did you ever see any good? Did any blessing ever pass by you?' He will say: 'No, by Allah, O Lord.' And the one of the people of Paradise who suffered the most hardship in the world will be brought and dipped once into Paradise. Then it will be said to him: 'O son of Adam! Did you ever see any hardship? Did any difficulty ever pass by you?' He will say: 'No, by Allah, O Lord! No hardship ever passed by me, nor did I ever see any difficulty.'"
"8001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hell will be brought on that Day with seventy thousand reins, and with each rein will be seventy thousand angels dragging it."
"8002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon people when the one who remains steadfast upon his religion among them will be like one holding a burning ember in his fist."
"8003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon people when a man will not care where he obtained his wealth from, whether from what is lawful or from what is unlawful."
"8004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon people when a man will call his cousin and his relative: 'Come to ease! Come to ease!' whereas Madinah would be better for them if only they knew. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, none of them will leave it out of aversion to it except that Allah will settle in it in his place someone better than him. Behold! Madinah is like a furnace that expels impurity. The Hour will not be established until Madinah expels its wicked people just as the furnace removes the impurity of iron."
"8005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon people when a group of people will go out on campaign and they will be asked: 'Is there among you a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?' They will say: 'Yes.' So victory will be opened for them. Then another time will come upon people when a group of people will go out on campaign and they will be asked: 'Is there among you a companion of a Companion?' They will say: 'Yes.' So victory will be opened for them. Then another time will come upon people when a group of people will go out on campaign and they will be asked: 'Is there among you a companion of a companion of a Companion?' They will say: 'Yes.' So victory will be opened for them."
"8006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times there will come a people young in age and foolish in mind. They will speak the best words of creation, yet they will pass out of Islam just as an arrow passes through the game. Their faith will not go beyond their throats. So kill them, for in killing them there is a reward on the Day of Resurrection for the one who kills them."
"8007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man is rewarded for all his spending except for spending on earth."
"8008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A mukatab (a slave who has contracted to buy his freedom) will receive the blood money of a free man in proportion to the amount of his freedom price that he has paid, and the blood money of a slave in proportion to what remains."
"8009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Compeller, will take His heavens and His earth in His Hand, then He will say: 'I am the Compeller, I am the King. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?'"
"8010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will eat and drink in it, but they will not blow their noses, nor relieve themselves, nor urinate. Rather, after their food there will only be belching and sweat like musk. Glorification and praise will be inspired in them just as breathing happens by itself."
"8011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the one who is the best reciter of the Book of Allah lead the people in prayer. If they are equal in recitation, then the one with the most knowledge of the Sunnah. If they are equal in the Sunnah too, then the one who was earliest in emigration (hijrah). If they are equal in emigration too, then the one oldest in age. And no man should lead another in prayer in his household or in his domain of authority, nor sit in his house on his special seat, except with his permission."
"8012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the one among them who is the best reciter of the Qur'an lead the people in prayer."
"8013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of you sees the speck in his brother's eye but forgets the log in his own eye."
"8014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be resurrected according to their intentions."
"8015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every servant will be resurrected in the state in which he died."
"8016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will be followed by seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan wearing striped shawls (tayalisah)."
"8017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things follow the deceased: his family, his deeds and his wealth. Two of them return and one remains: his family and his wealth return, and his deeds remain."
"8018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our Lord will manifest Himself to us, smiling, on the Day of Resurrection."
"8019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Angels by night and angels by day take turns among you, and they gather at the Fajr prayer and the Asr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and Allah asks them, although He knows those servants best: 'In what state did you leave My servants?' They say: 'We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying.'"
"8020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Time will draw close together, knowledge will be taken away, miserliness will be cast (into hearts), trials will appear and harj will increase. It was asked: 'What is harj?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Killing.'"
"8021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, and says: 'Who will call upon Me so that I may answer him? Who will ask of Me so that I may give him? Who will seek My forgiveness so that I may forgive him?'"
"8022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and thrown into the Fire, and his intestines will spill out, and he will go round with them in the Fire just as a donkey goes round its millstone. The people of the Fire will gather around him and say: 'O so-and-so! What has happened to you? Did you not use to command us to do good and forbid us from evil?' He will say: 'Yes, I used to command you to do good but did not do it myself, and I used to forbid you from evil but did it myself.'"
"8023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a group passes by, it suffices for all of them if one of them gives the greeting of salam, and it suffices for all of those seated if one of them returns it."
"8024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One mudd of water suffices for ablution (wudu), and one sa' suffices for the ritual bath (ghusl)."
"8025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will gather all people on one plain on the Day of Resurrection. Then the Lord of the worlds will appear to them and say: 'Should not every person follow what he used to worship?' So for the one who worshipped the cross his cross will be made to appear, for the one who worshipped images his images, and for the fire-worshipper his fire, and they will follow what they used to worship. Only the Muslims will remain. The Lord of the worlds will appear to them and say: 'Will you not follow the people?' They will say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from you, we seek refuge in Allah from you! Allah is our Lord, and we will stay in this place until we see our Lord.' He will command them and keep them firm. The Companions said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Will we see Him?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon?' They said: 'No.' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Then you will have no difficulty in seeing Him at that hour either.' Then He will conceal Himself, then He will appear and make Himself known to them, then He will say: 'I am your Lord, so follow Me.' So the Muslims will stand up, and the Sirat will be laid down, and they will pass over it like swift horses and camels, and their words upon it will be: 'Sallim, sallim (grant safety, grant safety).' And the people of Hell will remain. A group of them will be thrown into it, then it will be asked: 'Are you full?' It will say: 'Are there any more?' Then another group will be thrown in, and it will be asked: 'Are you full?' It will say: 'Are there any more?' Until, when all of them have been put into it, the Most Merciful will place His Foot in it and its parts will draw together, one onto another. Then He will say: 'Enough?' It will say: 'Enough, enough.' So when Allah has admitted the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of Hell into Hell, death will be brought, seized by the collar, and made to stand on the wall between the people of Paradise and the people of Hell. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise!' and they will look out, frightened. Then it will be said: 'O people of Hell!' and they will look out, happy, hoping for intercession. Then it will be said to the people of Paradise and the people of Hell: 'Do you recognise this?' Both groups will say: 'Yes, we recognise it; it is the death that was appointed over us.' So it will be laid down and slaughtered on the wall. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise! Now there is eternity, no death. And O people of Hell! Now there is eternity, no death.'"
"8026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believers will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection and, troubled by it, they will say: 'If only we could seek someone to intercede for us with our Lord so that He relieves us from this place of ours.' So they will go to Adam (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Adam! You are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His Hand, made His angels prostrate to you and taught you the names of all things, so intercede for us with your Lord so that He relieves us from this place of ours.' Adam (peace be upon him) will say: 'I am not fit for that' - and he will mention the error he committed and feel shy before his Lord because of it - and he will say: 'Rather, go to Nuh (peace be upon him), for he is the first Messenger whom Allah sent to the people of the earth.' So they will go to Nuh (peace be upon him) and he will say: 'I am not fit for that' - and he will mention to them his error of asking his Lord for something of which he had no knowledge, and he will feel shy before his Lord because of it - and he will say: 'Rather, go to Ibrahim, the Intimate Friend of the Most Merciful.' So they will go to him and he will say: 'I am not fit for that. Rather, go to Musa (peace be upon him), to whom Allah spoke directly and to whom He gave the Torah.' So they will go to Musa (peace be upon him) and he will say: 'I am not fit for that' - and he will mention to them the soul he killed without it having killed anyone, and he will feel shy before his Lord because of it - and he will say: 'Rather, go to Isa (peace be upon him), the servant of Allah and His Messenger, His Word and His Spirit.' So they will go to Isa (peace be upon him) and he will say: 'I am not fit for that. Rather, go to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), a servant whose past and future sins Allah has forgiven.' So I will rise and walk between two rows of believers until I seek permission from my Lord, and permission will be given to me. When I see my Lord, I will fall down in prostration before my Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, and He will leave me in that state for as long as He wills. Then He will say: 'O Muhammad! Raise your head. Speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a praise that He Himself will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return a second time, and when I see my Lord, I will fall down in prostration before my Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, and He will leave me in that state for as long as He wills. Then He will say: 'O Muhammad! Raise your head. Speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a praise that He Himself will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return a third time, and when I see my Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, I will fall down in prostration before my Lord, and He will leave me in that state for as long as He wills. Then He will say: 'O Muhammad! Raise your head. Speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So when I raise my head, I will praise my Lord with a praise that He Himself will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return a fourth time and say: 'O Lord! None remain except those whom the Qur'an has confined.' Then there will be taken out of Hell whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' (There is none truly worthy of worship except Allah) and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a grain of barley. Then there will be taken out of Hell whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a grain of wheat. Then there will be taken out of Hell whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a speck."
"8027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and when Paradise is brought near to the believers, they will stand up for intercession. They will go to Adam (peace be upon him) and say: 'O our father! Ask for Paradise to be opened for us.' He will say: 'Was it anything other than the error of your father Adam that expelled you from Paradise? I am not the one for this task. Go to my son Ibrahim, the Intimate Friend of Allah.' Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say: 'I am not the one for this task. I was only an intimate friend from far, far behind. Go to Musa (peace be upon him), to whom Allah spoke directly.' So they will go to Musa (peace be upon him) and he will say: 'I am not the one for this task. Go to Isa (peace be upon him), who is the Word of Allah and His Spirit.' Isa (peace be upon him) will say: 'I am not the one for this task. Go to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' So they will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and he will stand up for intercession and permission will be given to him. And trustworthiness and kinship will be sent forth, and they will stand on the right and left sides of the Sirat. The first of you will pass like lightning, then at the speed of the wind, then at the speed of a bird, then at the speed of swift runners, their deeds carrying them along. And your Prophet will be standing on the Sirat saying: 'O Lord! Grant safety, grant safety.' Until the deeds of the servants fall short, and a man will come who is unable to move except by crawling. And on both edges of the Sirat there will be hanging hooks, commanded to seize whomever they are ordered to seize. So some will be scratched but saved, and some will be thrown headlong into Hell."
"8028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will come and trample the whole earth except Makkah and Madinah. He will come to Madinah and find rows of angels at each of its passes. Then he will come to the salty plain of al-Jurf near Madinah and pitch his tent, and Madinah will shake with three tremors, and every hypocrite man and woman will go out to him."
"8029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man will come holding another man by the hand and say: 'O Lord! This man killed me.' Allah will ask the killer: 'Why did you kill him?' He will say: 'I killed him so that honour would be Yours.' Allah will say: 'Indeed, honour is Mine alone.' And another man will come holding a man by the hand and say: 'O Lord! This man killed me.' Allah will ask: 'Why did you kill him?' He will say: 'So that honour would be for so-and-so.' Allah will say: 'Honour does not belong to so-and-so.' So he will return bearing his sin."
"8030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an will come on the Day of Resurrection and say: 'O Lord! Adorn him.' So he will be made to wear the crown of honour. Then it will say: 'O Lord! Give him more.' So he will be made to wear the garment of honour. Then it will say: 'O Lord! Be pleased with him.' So Allah will be pleased with him. Then it will be said to that person: 'Recite and ascend,' and for every verse one good deed will be added."
"8031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The slain man will come with his killer on the Day of Resurrection, holding his forelock and head in his hand, with blood gushing from his veins, and he will say: 'O Lord! Ask this man why he killed me,' until he brings him near to the Throne."
"8032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The slain man will come on the Day of Resurrection clinging to his killer, and Allah will say: 'Why did you kill this man?' He will say: 'To strengthen the kingship of so-and-so.'"
"8033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prophet will come on the Day of Resurrection with only one man with him, and a prophet will come with two men with him, and a prophet will come with three or more with him. It will be said to him: 'Did you convey the message to your people?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then his people will be called and it will be said to them: 'Did he convey this message to you?' They will say: 'No.' Then it will be said to that prophet: 'Who will testify for you?' He will say: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Ummah.' So Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Ummah will be called, and it will be said to them: 'Did this prophet convey the message to his people?' They will say: 'Yes.' They will be asked: 'How do you know that?' They will say: 'Our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told us that all the Messengers had conveyed the message, and we believed him.' This is the meaning of Allah's saying: 'And thus We have made you the best nation, so that you may be witnesses over mankind and the Messenger may be a witness over you.'"
"8034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nuh (peace be upon him) and his nation will come, and Allah will ask: 'Did you convey the message?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord!' Then Allah will ask his nation: 'Did he convey the message to you?' They will say: 'No, no prophet came to us.' So Allah will say to Nuh (peace be upon him): 'Who will testify for you?' He will say: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Ummah.' And this is the saying of Allah Almighty: 'And thus We have made you the best nation, so that you may be witnesses over mankind' - and 'wasat' means just. So they will be called, and they will testify for him that he conveyed the message, then I will be a witness over you."
"8035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection some people from among the Muslims will come with sins like mountains; Allah will forgive them and place those sins upon the Jews."
"8036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Protection granted by even the lowest man of my Ummah is binding on behalf of the whole Ummah."
"8037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah loves that when a worker does a task, he does it excellently."
"8038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Breastfeeding makes unlawful the same relations that lineage makes unlawful."
"8039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Their betrayals, disobedience and lies will be reckoned, and the punishment you gave them will also be reckoned. If your punishment was equal to their sins, it will be even, neither in your favour nor against you. If your punishment was less than their sins, it will be a surplus in your favour. And if your punishment exceeded their sins, the surplus will be taken from you in their favour. Have you not read in the Book of Allah: 'And We will set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection' (to the end of the verse)?"
"8040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The arrogant will be raised on the Day of Resurrection like tiny ants but in the form of men. Humiliation will cover them from every side. They will be driven to a prison in Hell called Bulas. The fiercest of fires will rise over them, and they will be made to drink the tinat al-khabal, the fluid squeezed out of the bodies of the people of Hell."
"8041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be gathered in three ways: some eager and fearful; some two to a camel, three to a camel, four to a camel and ten to a camel; and the rest of them will be gathered by the Fire. It will take its midday rest with them where they take their midday rest, spend the night with them where they spend the night, be with them in the morning where they are in the morning, and be with them in the evening where they are in the evening."
"8042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be raised according to their intentions."
"8043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked and uncircumcised. The matter will be far too grave for them to look at one another."
"8044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection upon a white, reddish-tinged land like a loaf of pure bread, with no landmark on it for anyone."
"8045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three kinds of people attend the Friday prayer: one who attends it and engages in idle talk, and that is his share of it. The second is one who attends it and makes supplication; he is a man who has called upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: if Allah wills He grants him, and if He wills He withholds. The third is one who attends it in silence and calm, does not step over the neck of any Muslim and does not harm anyone; this becomes an expiation for his sins from that Friday until the next Friday, and three days more. That is because Allah says: Whoever comes with a good deed will have ten times the like of it."
"8046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The martyrs and those who died on their beds will dispute before our Lord about those who die of the plague. The martyrs will say: 'They are our brothers; they were killed just as we were killed.' And those who died on their beds will say: 'They are our brothers; they died on their beds just as we died.' So Allah will judge between them and will say: 'Look at their wounds; if their wounds resemble the wounds of those who were killed, then they are of them and with them.' So they will look at the wounds of those who died of the plague and will find that their wounds resemble the wounds of the martyrs, and they will be joined with the martyrs."
"8047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will emerge in my Ummah and will remain for forty. Then Allah Almighty will send Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon them both), who will resemble Urwah bin Mas'ud al-Thaqafi; he will seek him out and destroy him. Then people will live for seven years with no enmity even between two people. Then Allah will send a cold wind from the direction of Sham, and there will remain no one on the face of the earth with even a speck of faith in his heart except that the wind will take his soul, so much so that if one of you were to go inside a mountain, it would enter there too and take his soul. Then only the worst of people will remain, light-headed like birds and senseless like beasts of prey; they will neither recognise good nor reject evil. Then Satan will appear to them and say: 'Will you not obey me?' They will say: 'What do you command us?' So he will command them to worship idols, and they will begin worshipping them, and all the while their provision will be abundant and their life comfortable. Then the Trumpet will be blown, and no one will hear it except that he will incline one ear and raise the other. The first to hear it will be a man repairing the trough of his camels; he will fall unconscious, and all the people will fall unconscious. Then Allah will send rain like dew, from which people's bodies will grow. Then the Trumpet will be blown again, and they will all be standing, looking on. Then it will be said: 'O people, come to your Lord. And stop them; indeed they are to be questioned.' Then it will be said: 'Bring out the contingent of Hell.' It will be asked: 'Out of how many?' It will be said: 'Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.' That will be the Day that turns children grey-haired, and that will be the Day when the shin is uncovered."
"8048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will emerge, and a man from among the believers will set out towards him. The Dajjal's guards will meet him and say to him: 'Where are you heading?' He will say: 'I am going to this Dajjal who has emerged.' They will say: 'Do you not believe in our lord?' He will say: 'There is nothing hidden about the truth of our Lord.' They will say: 'Kill him.' Then they will say to one another: 'Has your lord not forbidden you to kill anyone without him?' So they will take him to the Dajjal. When the believer sees him, he will say: 'O people, this is the Dajjal whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned.' So the Dajjal will give orders concerning him and he will be laid out, and he will say: 'Seize him and wound him.' So his belly and back will be severely beaten. Then the Dajjal will say: 'Do you still not believe in me?' He will say: 'You are the false Messiah.' Then an order will be given concerning him, and he will be sawn with a saw from the middle of his head until he is split apart down to his legs. Then the Dajjal will walk between the two pieces and say to him: 'Stand up.' And he will stand up straight. Then he will say to him: 'Do you now believe in me?' He will say: 'My insight about you has only increased.' Then he will say: 'O people, after me he will not be able to do this to anyone else.' So the Dajjal will seize him intending to slaughter him, but the part from his neck to his shoulder will be made of copper, and he will find no way to get at him. So he will take him by his hands and feet and throw him; people will think that he was thrown into the Fire, whereas in reality he was cast into Paradise. This man will be the greatest of all people in testimony before the Lord of the worlds."
"8049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will emerge, and with him will be a river and a fire. Whoever enters his river, sin becomes binding upon him and his reward is removed; and whoever enters his fire, reward becomes due to him and his sin is removed. Then after that there will only be the establishment of the Hour."
"8050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah will bring some people out of Hell and admit them into Paradise."
"8051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection a neck will come out of Hell. It will have two eyes that see, two ears that hear and a tongue that speaks. It will say: 'I have been appointed over three kinds of people: over every obstinate tyrant, over everyone who called upon another deity besides Allah, and over the image-makers.'"
"8052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times, some people will emerge who are young in age and foolish in mind. They will recite the Qur'an with their tongues, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will speak the best words of creation. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game. So whoever meets them should kill them, for in killing them there is a great reward with Allah for the one who kills them."
"8053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will emerge among you such that you will consider your prayer insignificant compared to their prayer, your fasting compared to their fasting and your deeds compared to their deeds. They will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game, and it passes out so cleanly that the archer looks at the arrowhead and sees nothing, looks at its shaft and sees nothing, looks at its feathers and sees nothing, and looks doubtfully at its notch to see whether any trace of blood has clung to it."
"8054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times some people will emerge who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. Their mark will be shaving the head. When you meet them, kill them."
"8055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will be brought out of Hell through the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and admitted into Paradise, and they will be called the Jahannamiyyun (the people of Hell)."
"8056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will emerge from my Ummah who will recite the Qur'an; your recitation will be nothing compared to their recitation, nor your prayer compared to their prayer, nor your fasting compared to their fasting. They will recite the Qur'an thinking that it is in their favour, whereas it will be against them. Their prayer will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of Islam just as an arrow passes through the game. If the army that confronts them knew what reward has been decreed for them for killing them upon the tongue of their Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), they would rely on that and give up doing deeds. And the sign of this group is that among them will be a man who has an upper arm but no forearm; at the end of his upper arm there will be something like the nipple of a breast, with white hairs on it."
"8057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will emerge from the East with shaven heads. They will recite the Qur'an with their tongues, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game."
"8058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four men will be brought out of Hell and presented before Allah. One of them will turn towards Allah and say: 'O my Lord, since You have brought me out of it, do not return me to it.' So Allah will save him from it."
"8059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will be brought out of Hell through intercession looking like tha'arir (small white cucumbers)."
"8060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will be brought out of Hell after they have been burnt, and admitted into Paradise, and the people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamiyyun (the people of Hell)."
"8061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true deity except Allah) and had in his heart good equal to even the weight of a grain of barley will be brought out of Hell. Then whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a grain of wheat will be brought out. Then whoever said 'La ilaha illallah' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a speck will be brought out."
"8062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has even a speck's weight of faith in his heart will be brought out of Hell."
"8063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will emerge from the direction of the East who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game, and then they will never return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Their mark will be shaving the head."
"8064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ka'bah will be destroyed by the man from Abyssinia with two thin shins."
"8065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hand of Allah is over the Jama'ah (the united community)."
"8066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hand of Allah is full; spending does not diminish it, and He spends lavishly night and day. Have you seen how much He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? Yet it has not diminished what is in His Hand. His Throne was upon the water, and in His Hand is the Scale; He decreases and increases provision."
"8067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand of the giver is the upper hand. Begin with those for whom you are responsible: your mother, your father, your sister and your brother, then whoever is closest to you, and then the next closest. Indeed, no soul will bear the burden of another soul's sin."
"8068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will enter Paradise whose hearts are soft like the hearts of birds."
"8069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Through the intercession of one man from my Ummah, more people than the number of the tribe of Banu Tamim will enter Paradise."
"8070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group from my Ummah will enter Paradise, and they will be seventy thousand. Their faces will shine like the moon on the night of the full moon."
"8071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not ask for ruqyah, do not take bad omens and do not have themselves cauterised, and who put their trust in their Lord."
"8072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless and beardless, with kohl-lined eyes, as young people of thirty-three years of age."
"8073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will be admitted into Paradise and the people of Hell into Hell. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'Bring out whoever has faith in his heart equal to even the weight of a mustard seed.' So they will be brought out of Hell, having turned black, and will be cast into the River of Life, and they will sprout just as a seed sprouts at the edge of a flood stream. Have you not seen that it comes out yellow and twisted?"
"8074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of Hell into Hell. Then a caller will stand between them and say: 'O people of Paradise, there is no more death! And O people of Hell, there is no more death! Each will abide forever in the place where he is.'"
"8075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angel comes to the drop of semen forty days after it settles in the womb and says: 'O Lord, what shall I write? Wretched or fortunate? Male or female?' Then Allah speaks, and the angels write it down, and his deeds, his end, his affliction, his provision and the time of his death are written. Then the scroll is rolled up, and nothing is added to what is in it nor taken away."
"8076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poor Muslims will enter Paradise half a day before their wealthy ones, and that half day will be five hundred years."
"8077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam will fade away just as the embroidery of a garment fades, until people will not even know what fasting is, what prayer is, what Hajj is and what charity is. And the Book of Allah will be taken away in a single night, so that not a single verse of it will remain on the earth. Some groups of people will remain, old men and old women, who will say: 'We found our forefathers upon this word; they used to say 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true deity except Allah), so we say it too.'"
"8078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The righteous will depart one after another, and there will remain worthless people, like the leftover refuse of barley or dates. Allah Almighty will not care about them at all."
"8079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the mother of Isma'il (peace be upon him)! Had she left Zamzam to flow as it was, or he said: had she not scooped up its water by the handful, it would have been a flowing spring."
"8080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the mother of Isma'il (peace be upon him)! Had she not been hasty, Zamzam would have been a flowing spring."
"8081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will come to Hell by way of the Bridge (Sirat), then they will pass over it according to their deeds. The first of them will pass like the blink of an eye, then like the speed of the wind, then like the gallop of a horse, then like a man riding his mount, then like a man running fast, then like one walking normally."
"8082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection some people from among my Companions will come to me, and they will be driven away from the Pool. I will say: 'O Lord, these are my Companions!' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you; after you they turned back on their heels.'"
"8083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Weeping will be sent upon the people of Hell, and they will weep until their tears run out. Then they will weep blood until it flows on their faces like channels; if ships were set sailing in them, they would sail."
"8084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People ask me about the Hour, whereas its knowledge is only with Allah. And I swear by Allah that no living soul on the earth today will complete a hundred years."
"8085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of any one of you continues to be answered as long as he is not hasty and does not say: 'I supplicated, but my supplication was not answered.'"
"8086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give glad tidings and do not drive people away."
"8087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give glad tidings and do not drive people away; and cooperate with each other and do not differ."
"8088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should greet the one walking, the one walking should greet the one standing, and the few should greet the many."
"8089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should greet the one walking, the one walking should greet the one sitting, and the few should greet the many."
"8090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The younger should greet the elder, the one passing by should greet the one sitting, and the few should greet the many."
"8091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will drink wine, but they will call it by another name."
"8092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will drink wine and will call it by a name other than its real name."
"8093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The martyr will intercede for seventy people of his household."
"8094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A supplication should be made for the one who sneezes three times; if it is more than that, then he has a cold."
"8095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from my Ummah will be called out on the Day of Resurrection before all of creation, and ninety-nine registers will be spread open before him, each register stretching as far as the eye can see. Then Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will say: Do you reject anything of this? He will say: No, O Lord. Allah will say: Have My guardian angels who record wronged you? He will say: No, O Lord. Then Allah will say: Do you have any excuse? Do you have any good deed? The man will be overawed and say: No. Allah will say: Indeed you do; you have a good deed with Us, and no injustice will be done to you today. Then a card will be brought out for him on which is written: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger). He will say: O Lord! What is this card compared to these registers? Allah will say: You will not be wronged. Then the registers will be placed in one pan of the scale and the card in the other pan, and the registers will become light and the card will become heavy."
"8096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every morning charity is due on every joint of the son of Adam: greeting whomever one meets is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, removing something harmful from the path is charity, and having intimate relations with one's wife is also charity. And two rak'ahs of the forenoon (Duha) prayer suffice for all of this."" The Companions said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If one of us fulfils his desire, will he also receive the reward of charity?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell me, if he were to use it in an unlawful place, would he not incur sin?"
"8097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every morning charity is due on every joint of each one of you: every glorification (tasbih) is charity, every praise (tahmid) is charity, every declaration of Allah's oneness (tahlil) is charity, every declaration of His greatness (takbir) is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and two rak'ahs of the forenoon (Duha) prayer that you pray suffice for all of this."
"8098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every day charity is due on every joint of each one of you. So for every prayer he receives the reward of charity, for every fast the reward of charity, for every Hajj the reward of charity, for every tasbih the reward of charity, for every takbir the reward of charity and for every tahmid the reward of charity; and two rak'ahs of the forenoon (Duha) prayer suffice each one of you for all of this."
"8099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those rulers will lead you in prayer. If they do it correctly, the reward is for you; and if they err, the reward is for you and the burden of it is upon them."
"8100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, and both enter Paradise: this one fights in the path of Allah and is killed; then Allah accepts the repentance of the killer, so he becomes a Muslim, then he fights in the path of Allah and is martyred."
"8101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah will fold up the heavens on the Day of Resurrection, then take them in His right hand, then say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? Then He will fold up the earths, then take them in His left hand, then say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?"
"8102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your Lord is amazed at a shepherd of goats on the peak of a mountain who calls the adhan for the prayer and prays. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Look at this servant of Mine; he calls the adhan and establishes the prayer, fearing Me. I have forgiven My servant and admitted him into Paradise."
"8103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some of the people of Tawhid (monotheism) will be punished; they will be thrown into Hell until they become charcoal in it. Then mercy will reach them, and they will be taken out and thrown at the gates of Paradise. The people of Paradise will sprinkle water on them, and they will sprout just as something sprouts in the debris carried by a flood. Then they will enter Paradise."
"8104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will sweat so much on the Day of Resurrection that their sweat will sink seventy cubits deep into the earth, and it will reach their ears and bridle them like a rein."
"8105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does one of you bite his brother as a male camel bites?! There is no blood money (diyah) for him."
"8106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer will be given in Paradise the strength of a hundred men with regard to women."
"8107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sleeps, Satan ties three knots at the back of his head, saying at each knot: You have a long night ahead, so sleep on. If he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is untied; if he performs ablution (wudu), another knot is untied; and if he prays, all the knots are untied. So he begins the morning energetic and in good spirits; otherwise he begins the morning in bad spirits and lazy."
"8108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Aqiqah should be performed for a boy, and his head should not be smeared with blood."
"8109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Would one of you deliberately take a live coal of fire and put it in his hand?"
"8110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does one of you sit down in his prayer the way a camel sits down?!"
"8111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does one of you beat his wife as a slave is beaten, and then perhaps lie with her at the end of that same day?"
"8112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does Satan come to one of you and frighten him (in a dream), and then he gets up in the morning and goes about telling people (that dream)?!"
"8113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One seeking refuge will seek refuge in the House (of Allah), and an army will be sent against him. When they reach a stretch of open desert land, they will be swallowed up by the earth."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about the one who was unwilling?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He will be swallowed up along with them, but on the Day of Resurrection he will be raised according to his intention."
"8114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An army will attack the Ka'bah, and when they reach a stretch of open desert land, the first and the last of them will all be swallowed up by the earth. Then they will be raised according to their intentions."
"8115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An army will attack this House (the Ka'bah), and they will be swallowed up by the earth in the open desert."
"8116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from a vessel, it should be washed seven times, the last or the first of them with earth; and when a cat laps from a vessel, it should be washed once."
"8117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(Clothing) should be washed from the urine of a girl, and (water) should be sprinkled on the urine of a boy."
"8118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He gets angry with me because I cannot find anything to give him! Whoever among you asks while he has an uqiyah or its equivalent has asked importunately."
"8119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every sin of the martyr is forgiven except debt."
"8120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It will be said to the people of Paradise: O people of Paradise! (Now there is) eternity, no death. And it will be said to the people of Hell: O people of Hell! (Now there is) eternity, no death."
"8121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the companion of the Qur'an enters Paradise, it will be said to him: Recite and ascend. So he will recite and ascend, (rising) one level for every verse, until he recites the last thing he has with him (the last verse)."
"8122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an: Recite, ascend and recite slowly and distinctly, as you used to recite slowly and distinctly in the world, for your rank will be at the last verse you used to recite."
"8123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection it will be said to a man from the people of Hell: Tell me, if you had everything on the earth, would you give it as a ransom (for your deliverance)? He will say: Yes. Then Allah Almighty will say: You have lied. I asked of you something easier than that. I took a covenant from you while you were in the loins of Adam (peace be upon him) that you would not associate anything with Me, but you refused to do anything but associate partners with Me."
"8124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Knowledge will be taken away, ignorance and trials will appear, and killing will increase."
"8125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold up the heavens in His right hand, then He will say: I am the King; where are the kings of the earth?"
"8126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Maryam (Isa, peace be upon him) will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"8127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one in ihram may kill the biting dog, the mouse, the scorpion, the kite and the crow."
"8128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A donkey, a woman and a dog interrupt the prayer."
"8129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A menstruating woman and a black dog interrupt the prayer."
"8130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman, a donkey and a dog interrupt the prayer, and (placing something as a sutrah) the size of the back of a camel saddle protects against that."
"8131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When there is nothing in front of a man the size of the back of a camel saddle, a woman, a donkey and a black dog interrupt his prayer; the black dog is a devil."
"8132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth! (Yet) O son of Adam, your share of your wealth is only what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent ahead."
"8133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The servant says: My wealth, my wealth! Yet his share of his wealth is only three things: what he ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave away and sent ahead. Everything other than that is departing, and he will leave it behind for the people."
"8134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection the servant will say: O my Lord! Did You not grant me protection from injustice? Allah Almighty will say: Indeed. He will say: Then I will not accept any witness against myself except one from myself. Allah Almighty will say: Sufficient is your own self against you today as a reckoner, and the noble recording angels as witnesses. Then a seal will be placed upon his mouth, and it will be said to his limbs: Speak! So they will speak about his deeds. Then he will be allowed to speak, and he will say: Away with you and perish! It was on your behalf that I was contending (in defence)."
"8135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: The one who strives (in jihad) in My path is under My guarantee. If I take him (as a martyr), I will grant him Paradise, and if I return him, I will return him with reward or spoils."
"8136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"8137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me in himself, I remember him in Myself; and if he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than it. If he draws near to Me by a hand-span, I draw near to him by a forearm's length; if he draws near to Me by a forearm's length, I draw near to him by an arm's span; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"8138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. By Allah! Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you who finds his lost property in the wilderness. Whoever draws near to Me by a hand-span, I draw near to him by a forearm's length; whoever draws near to Me by a forearm's length, I draw near to him by an arm's span; and if he comes towards Me walking, I come towards him running."
"8139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: My believing servant has no reward with Me, when I take away his dear one from the people of this world and he then bears it patiently hoping for reward, except Paradise."
"8140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Whoever I deprive of his two beloved things (his eyes), and he is patient and hopes for reward, I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise."
"8141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Whoever does a good deed will have ten times its like (and even more), and whoever does an evil deed, its recompense is its equal, or I forgive. Whoever meets Me with an earth-full of sins, having associated nothing with Me, I will grant him an equal amount of forgiveness. Whoever draws near to Me by a handspan, I draw near to him by a forearm's length; whoever draws near to Me by a forearm's length, I draw near to him by an arm-span; and whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"8142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will say: O Adam! He will reply: Here I am, and all good is in Your hands. Allah Almighty will say: Bring out the portion destined for the Fire. Adam (peace be upon him) will ask: What is the portion destined for the Fire? Allah Almighty will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. At that time the young child will turn grey, every pregnant woman will miscarry, and you will see people as if intoxicated, though they will not be intoxicated; rather, the punishment of Allah is severe. The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, then which of us will be that one? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Rejoice, for from you there will be one man and from Gog and Magog a thousand. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be a quarter of the people of Paradise; I hope that you will be a third of the people of Paradise; I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. Among people (compared to the other nations) you are only like a black hair on the hide of a white ox, or a white hair on the hide of a black ox, or (the size of) a mark on the foreleg of a donkey."
"8143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! When I take away your two dear things (your eyes), and you are patient and hope for reward at the first shock, I am not pleased with any reward for you less than Paradise."
"8144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! How can you render Me helpless when I created you from something like this (a drop of fluid)? Then, when I had fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked about wearing two cloaks and the earth thudded beneath your steps. Then you gathered (wealth) and withheld it, until, when (your soul) reached the throat, you said: Now I will give charity. But where is the time for charity now?!"
"8145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People call (the grapevine) 'karm', whereas the true karm (nobility) is the heart of the believer."
"8146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of them will stand in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"8147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let each of you shield his face from the heat of Hell, even with a date or with half a date, for each of you will meet Allah, and Allah will say to him just what I am saying to one of you: Did I not give you hearing and sight? He will say: Yes indeed. Allah will say: Did I not give you wealth and children? He will say: Yes indeed. Allah will say: What have you sent ahead for yourself? He will look in front of him, behind him, to his right and to his left, and will find nothing with which to shield his face from the heat of Hell. So let each of you shield his face from the Fire (of Hell), even with half a date, and if he does not find (even) that, then with a good word. I do not fear poverty and want for you, for Allah will help you and give you (blessings), until a woman will travel alone between Yathrib and al-Hirah, and the most that will be feared for her mount is theft."
"8148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be rulers over you who will delay the prayer; it will count for you and (its burden) will be on them. So pray with them as long as they lead you in prayer facing the Qiblah."
"8149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last days there will be (occurrences of) the swallowing up by the earth, pelting (with stones from the sky), and the transformation of faces."
"8150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last days there will be a caliph who will distribute wealth and will not even count it."
"8151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last days there will be deceivers and liars who will bring you narrations that neither you nor your forefathers have heard. So beware of them, lest they lead you astray and put you to trial."
"8152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Whatever part is cut from a living animal is (in the ruling of) carrion."
"8153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last days there will be people who will dye (their hair) with black like the breasts of pigeons; they will not even smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"8154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At the end of my Ummah there will be a caliph who will scatter wealth by the handful and will not give it out by counting."
"8155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In my Ummah there will be (occurrences of) the swallowing up by the earth, the transformation of faces, and pelting (with stones from the sky)."
"8156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At the end of this Ummah there will be (occurrences of) the swallowing up by the earth, the transformation of faces, and pelting (with stones from the sky). It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, when evil becomes (openly) widespread."
"8157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be twelve leaders, all of them from Quraysh."
"8158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will meet his father Azar on the Day of Resurrection, and on Azar's face there will be darkness and dust. Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say to him: Did I not tell you not to disobey me? His father will say: Today I will not disobey you. Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say: O my Lord! You promised me that You would not disgrace me on the Day they are resurrected, and what disgrace could be greater than that my father is the farthest (from mercy)? Allah Almighty will say: I have forbidden Paradise to the disbelievers. Then it will be said: O Ibrahim! Look beneath your feet! He will look, and there will be a blood-smeared hyena, which will be seized by its legs and thrown into the Fire."
"8159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa (peace be upon him) will be inspired with his argument in this verse: And when Allah will say: O Isa son of Maryam! Did you say to people: Take me and my mother as two gods besides Allah? Then Allah will inspire him (with the answer): Glory be to You! It is not for me to say that to which I have no right, the whole verse."
"8160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from my household will rule whose name will match my name. If there remained of this world only a single day, Allah would lengthen that day until he comes to rule."
"8161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Muhajir may stay in Makkah for three days after completing the rites of his Hajj (or Umrah)."
"8162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blessing in horses lies in their red (sorrel) colour."
"8163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your oath is valid according to that on which your companion believes you."
"8164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A caller will call out: It is (the glad tidings) for you that you will now be healthy forever and never fall ill; it is for you that you will now live forever and never die; it is for you that you will now be young forever and never grow old; and it is for you that you will now live in bliss forever and never suffer hardship."
"8165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every night, when the first third of the night has passed, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and says: I am the King, I am the King! Who is there who will call upon Me so that I may answer him? Who is there who will ask of Me so that I may give him? Who is there who will seek My forgiveness so that I may forgive him? And this continues until the dawn becomes bright."
"8166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last third of the night Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and says: Who is there who will call upon Me so that I may answer him, or ask of Me so that I may give him? Then He spreads out His two hands and says: Who will lend to Me, while I am neither destitute nor unjust?"
"8167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every night Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and says: Is there anyone asking, that I may give him? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Is there anyone repenting, that I may accept his repentance? This continues until the break of dawn."
"8168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every night our Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, and says: Who is there who will call upon Me so that I may answer him? Who is there who will ask of Me so that I may give him? Who is there who will seek My forgiveness so that I may forgive him?"
"8169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon them both) will descend by the white minaret to the east of Damascus."
"8170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will settle in a low-lying land which they will call Basrah, by a river called the Tigris, over which there will be a bridge. Its inhabitants will be many, and it will be one of the cities of the Muslims. Then in the last days the Banu Qanturah will come, a people with broad faces and small eyes, until they encamp on the bank of the river. Its inhabitants will then split into three groups: one group will take hold of the tails of cattle and the wilderness, and they will perish; one group will (make terms) for their own lives, and they will disbelieve; and one group will put their children behind their backs and fight them, and they will be the martyrs."
"8171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A generation will arise who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. Whenever a group of them emerges it will be cut off; whenever a group emerges it will be cut off, until the Dajjal emerges among their remnants."
"8172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(Water) is to be sprinkled on the urine of a baby boy, and the urine of a baby girl is to be washed."
"8173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam grows old, but two things remain with him: greed and hope."
"8174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam grows old, but two things in him stay young (and fresh): greed for wealth and greed for (a long) life."
"8175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This tribe of Quraysh will destroy the people. The Companions said: Then what do you command us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If only the people would keep away from them."
"8176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Madinah are to enter ihram from Dhul-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, the people of Najd from Qarn, and the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."
"8177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, when the people of affliction are given their reward, the people of well-being will wish that their skins had been cut with scissors in the world."
"8178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon one of you will start praying the Fajr prayer as four rak'ahs."
"8179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the Euphrates (river) will uncover a mountain of gold. When people hear of it, they will set out towards it, and whoever is near it will say: By Allah! If we let the people take from it, they will carry it all away. So they will fight one another over it until ninety-nine out of every hundred are killed."
"8180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the Euphrates will uncover a treasure of gold, so whoever is present there should not take anything from it."
"8181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the Muslims will be besieged into Madinah, until their farthest outpost will be Salah."
"8182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon people will keep questioning one another until one of them says: This is Allah, who created the creation; then who created Allah? When they say that, recite: Allah is One; Allah is the Self-Sufficient; He neither begets nor was He begotten; and there is none equal to Him. Then let him spit dryly to his left three times and seek refuge (with Allah) from Satan."
"8183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the (hostile) nations will fall upon you from every side, just as diners fall upon their dish. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be few in number on that day? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, but you will be (worthless) like the scum of a flood. Weakness (wahn) will be put into your hearts, and awe of you will be removed from the hearts of your enemy, because you love the world and hate death."
"8184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If your life is prolonged, you will soon see people with things like the tails of cattle in their hands; they will go out in the morning under the wrath of Allah and return in the evening under the displeasure of Allah."
"8185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will come a time in which people will be thoroughly sifted, and only the dregs of people will remain, whose covenants and trusts will have become confused, and they will differ like this - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers. The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, what should we do then? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Adopt what you recognise (as good), leave what you do not recognise (as evil), attend to your own particular affairs, and leave the affairs of the general public."
"8186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon a man will be sitting reclining on his couch, and a narration of mine will be related to him, and he will say: Between us and you there is only the Book of Allah (to judge); whatever we find lawful in it we will treat as lawful, and whatever we find unlawful in it we will treat as unlawful. Beware! Whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has made unlawful is just like what Allah has made unlawful."
"8187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the best wealth of a Muslim will be goats, with which he follows the mountain peaks and the places where rain falls, fleeing from trials (to keep) his religion (safe)."
"8188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! If your life is prolonged, you will soon see this place here filled with gardens."
"8189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Sirat (bridge) will be placed across the middle of Hell, with thorns on it like the thorns of the sa'dan (a thorny plant). Then people will pass over it: some will be saved unharmed, some will be saved after being scratched, then some will be saved, some will be caught (in the thorns), and some will fall headlong into it."
"8190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Friday has twelve hours; among them is an hour in which no Muslim servant asks Allah for anything but that Allah certainly gives it to him. So seek it in the last hour after Asr."
"8191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The day of the Greater Hajj is the day of sacrifice (the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah)."
"8192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of sacrifice and the days of Tashriq are the days of Eid for us, the people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"8193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Day of Resurrection will be for the believers (as light) as the length of time between Zuhr and Asr."
"8194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An orphan girl is to be consulted about her (marriage); if she remains silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, (the marriage) is not permissible over her."
"8195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and (in spending) begin with those who are under your care."
"8196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those who are under your care. The best charity is that which is given while one is in a state of affluence. Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah makes him self-sufficient, and whoever seeks chastity (by refraining from begging), Allah grants him chastity."
"8197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand; the upper hand is the one that spends and the lower hand is the one that asks."
"8198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath is (valid) according to that on which your companion believes you."
"8199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath is according to the intention of the one who demands the oath."
"8200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Promised Day is the Day of Resurrection, the Witness (shahid) is the day of Friday, and the Witnessed (mashhud, that which is attended) is the day of Arafah. Allah has reserved the day of Friday especially for us, and the middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"8201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Promised Day is the Day of Resurrection, the Witnessed Day is the day of Arafah, and the Witness is the day of Friday. The sun has not risen nor set upon any day better than it. In it there is an hour such that no Muslim servant happens upon it, asking Allah for some good, except that Allah surely answers him, and he does not seek refuge from any evil except that Allah surely grants him refuge from it."
"8202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Jews are those upon whom is wrath (maghdub alayhim), and the Christians are those astray (dallin)."
